    "semantics": [
      "Every original Frames function body is retained as FrameFunc.Run at the original construction site; no gameplay callback is evaluated during observation.",
      "Default Dash captures original length and dashJumpLength; default Walk captures the original selected f including source fallback 1.",
      "Classic ordinary Jump captures the f from the original single JumpLength call. Fixed Xianyun/Stellar-airborne closures capture low/high plunge and fallback animation frames chosen by the original branch.",
      "Stellar ordinary Jump retains the live short-circuit JumpModified/Airborne predicate in Run. Observe reads both live values with pure Index/Airborne getters and copies the already captured frame lengths. No StatusIsActive, Duration, SetAirborne, JumpLength or Stat call is added to observation.",
      "JumpModifiedF is not consumed by this frame callback and is not invented as a dependency. Existing Stellar jump event and character/player phase providers retain their own state coverage.",
      "The delayed dash task uses the original captured parameter map at execution. Observe copies its current contents while preserving nil, so future mutations do not rewrite historical observations.",
      "The original single DashLength()-1 scheduling expression, task callback and execution order are retained. AddWithPhase uses the same task.add implementation as Add.",
      "AbilStamCost, StamPercentMod callbacks, ActionStam dispatch and UseStam remain at execution time only. This descriptor does not claim custom character or modifier state has become complete.",
      "Custom character movement implementations are not edited; unknown overrides and other callbacks remain opaque."
    ],
